 country right  now in the uk  there is very limited  official requirement for mask use at  least in england very little official  requirement for physical distancing and  very little official requirement for  hygiene  and yet  in wha we know that those are the most  effective ways of stopping this virus  from spreading  so it seems kind of odd that on the one  hand the uk is not following the  official guidance on what you do to  reduce covet spread but on the other  hand is saying we're going to move very  quickly to shut our borders when  certainly from the who side we have not  recommended that kind of action at all  so would you say that this is an  inefficient response and and not the  right one um given that the very basics  and to be honest you're not the first  expert i've spoken to on air over the  past few weeks who are saying the united  kingdom needs to go back to the basics  hands face space would you say that this  is an inefficient and  potentially  response that won't work  so i'm terribly careful not to make  remarks that appear to be critical of  any government but i am perfectly  prepared to encourage government action  where i think it's right  all over europe now the correct action  is that everybody should be wearing  well-fitted face masks at all times but  especially indoors and everybody should  be doing everything possible to avoid  breathing in air that is exhaled by  other people everyone should be  practicing really good hygiene  there should be good ventilation in  confined spaces and yes people should  get vaccinated if they're in the age  group that will benefit  we've got to do all these things this  virus is just unforgiving it is brutal  and it's coming back into europe with a  vengeance so please yes could we do  everything with regard to comments about  what's sorry do continue sorry  i just want to say that in general with  regard to decisions about flights from  southern africa  i just want to be very clear that as  soon as you start doing these kinds of  restrictions or travel bans  you're also having an impact on the  economy of countries that southern  african nations have been badly hit by  covid  they do not have  much room to be able to provide  extra support to people whose income  might be reduced because of unemployment  or other factors due to decisions taken  by other nations so just everybody when  you're going ahead and introducing these  kinds of unilateral travel restrictions  or whether it's for people from a  particular nation or for people who are  not vaccinated or whatever  please think of the human consequences  please speak to the people concerned  before you introduce the things because  we're all interdependent this pandemic  is everywhere and it's really  unfortunate when countries or groups of  countries act in a particular possibly  single-handed way without consulting  with others and i assume that also  applies to vaccines i'm afraid we're  going to have to leave it there david  nabarro i'm sure our viewers would love  to hear more from you thanks very much

